-    "content": "# [Guide] Legacy Tracker Migration and Cutover Runbook\n\n## Overview\n\nOrganizations seeking to escape SaaS paywalls, Jira seat taxes, and single-vendor agent lock-in require a safe, deterministic migration path. Legacy project management tools often store data in proprietary formats, making manual migration prone to data loss, dropped comments, and broken ticket linkages.\n\n\ud83d\udc4dkanban provides a battle-tested **7-Phase Live Cutover Protocol** (`docs/CUTOVER.md`) designed for migrating from legacy issue trackers (such as Jira, Vibe Kanban, or self-hosted boards) to \ud83d\udc4dkanban with zero data loss and minimal operational disruption.\n\n---\n\n## The 7-Phase Live Cutover Protocol\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    P1[\"Phase 1: Pre-Cutover Readiness & Schema Alignment<br/>- Deploy target stack, configure Multi-Card Auth<br/>- Run healthchecks and verify checksums\"]\n    P2[\"Phase 2: Read-Only Freeze of Source Platform<br/>- Place legacy tracker in maintenance mode<br/>- Capture baseline snapshot\"]\n    P3[\"Phase 3: Extraction & Markdown Normalization<br/>- Ingest JSON/XML export<br/>- Run Unicode Surrogate & Paste-Jacking pipeline\"]\n    P4[\"Phase 4: Universal Object Graph Hydration & Linking<br/>- Populate UOG spine & typed object_links<br/>- Generate redirect aliases\"]\n    P5[\"Phase 5: Six Non-Bypassable Verification Gates<br/>- Entity counts, Link Auditor, Markdown fidelity,<br/>ACL parity, MCP health, SLA latency\"]\n    P6[\"Phase 6: DNS Cutover & Traffic Switch<br/>- Point domain to \ud83d\udc4dkanban Caddy ingress\"]\n    P7[\"Phase 7: Post-Cutover Monitoring & Rollback Window<br/>- 7-day read-only fallback window\"]\n\n    P1 --> P2\n    P2 --> P3\n    P3 --> P4\n    P4 --> P5\n    P5 -->|Certified PASSED| P6\n    P6 --> P7\n```\n\n![Standalone to Production Compose Export](images/27-standalone-compose-export.png)\n\n### Phase 1: Pre-Cutover Readiness and Schema Alignment\n- Deploy target \ud83d\udc4dkanban production stack.\n- Configure Multi-Card Authentication cards to match source identity providers (OIDC/SAML/LDAP).\n- Run migration pre-flight checks: `uv run kanban-ctl ops healthcheck` and verify source export snapshot checksums (`sha256sum -c manifest.sha256`).\n\n### Phase 2: Read-Only Freeze of Source Platform\n- Place the legacy tracker instance into read-only maintenance mode.\n- Notify engineering teams and pause active CI/CD webhooks.\n- Capture baseline snapshot of source database.\n\n### Phase 3: Extraction and Markdown Normalization\n- Extract work items, cycles, modules, pages, stickies, and attachments via source tracker export APIs.\n- Pass all textual descriptions and comments through the \ud83d\udc4dkanban **Canonical Markdown Pipeline**:\n  - Rejects Unicode lone surrogates.\n  - Strips hidden DOM paste-jacking sequences.\n  - Converts legacy HTML into clean, standardized CommonMark.\n\n### Phase 4: Universal Object Graph Hydration\n- Ingest normalized objects into the PostgreSQL Universal Object Graph (`kanban_migrator`).\n- Translate legacy issue references (`PROJ-123`) into canonical \ud83d\udc4dkanban identifiers while creating redirect aliases.\n- Establish typed `object_links` for all parent-child relationships, sub-issues, and blockers.\n\n### Phase 5: The Six Non-Bypassable Verification Gates\nBefore DNS can be redirected, the migration must pass all 6 automated verification gates:\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    Gate1[\"Gate 1<br/>Entity Parity\"] --> Gate2[\"Gate 2<br/>Link Auditor\"]\n    Gate2 --> Gate3[\"Gate 3<br/>Markdown Fidelity\"]\n    Gate3 --> Gate4[\"Gate 4<br/>ACL Parity\"]\n    Gate4 --> Gate5[\"Gate 5<br/>MCP Health\"]\n    Gate5 --> Gate6[\"Gate 6<br/>SLA Latency\"]\n    Gate6 --> Cutover[\"Ready for Live Cutover\"]\n```\n\n| Gate # | Verification Gate | Success Threshold |\n| :---: | :--- | :--- |\n| **1** | **Entity Count Parity** | 100% match across issues, states, cycles, modules, comments, and attachments. |\n| **2** | **Object Link Auditor** | Zero orphaned links, cross-tenant leaks, or invalid hierarchy cycles. |\n| **3** | **Markdown Fidelity** | 100% of descriptions render valid Markdown; zero unparsed HTML tags. |\n| **4** | **Principal & ACL Parity** | All users, groups, and permissions map accurately to \ud83d\udc4dkanban roles. |\n| **5** | **MCP Surface Health** | All 24 MCP tools return clean schemas and pass handshake benchmarks. |\n| **6** | **Performance Latency** | Board view initial load under 100ms; REST API p95 latency under 50ms. |\n\n### Phase 6: DNS Cutover and Traffic Switch\n- Update internal DNS records or reverse proxy routing (e.g. Caddy / Nginx) to point domain `kanban.example.com` to the \ud83d\udc4dkanban production ingress (`edge_net`).\n- Restart agent background workers with updated MCP endpoint URLs.\n\n### Phase 7: Post-Cutover Monitoring and Rollback Window\n- Maintain legacy tracker instance in read-only state for a 7-day observation window.\n- Monitor real-time WebSocket connection stability and activity logs.\n\n---\n\n## Plane Migration Import Studio (`/admin/imports`)\n\nTo streamline cutover from Plane workspaces to \ud83d\udc4dkanban without custom extraction scripts, \ud83d\udc4dkanban includes a native **Plane Migration Import Studio** accessible at `/admin/imports` (and `/settings/mcp` -> Plane Migration Studio tab).\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    subgraph PlaneImportPipeline[\"Plane Migration Studio Pipeline\"]\n        Upload[\"Step 1: Upload Plane Export Bundle<br/>(File upload or paste raw JSON)\"] --> Parse[\"JSON Schema Validation<br/>Verify projects, states, issues, cycles, modules, comments, members\"]\n        Parse --> Metrics[\"Step 2: Entity Detection & Metrics Cards<br/>Live counts across all 7 entity types\"]\n        Metrics --> DryRun[\"Step 3: Stage 1 Dry-Run Simulation<br/>Idempotency checks, state mapping preview, conflict detection\"]\n        DryRun --> Live[\"Step 4: Execute Live Migration<br/>Atomic PostgreSQL transaction (kanban_migrator)\"]\n        Live --> Verify[\"Step 5: Post-Import Integrity Audit<br/>Run Invalid Object Link Auditor on imported graph\"]\n    end\n```\n\n![Plane Migration Import Studio Step 1](images/49-admin-plane-import-studio.png)\n\n![Plane Migration Studio Dry-Run Simulation](images/71-plane-migration-dry-run.png)\n\n### Key Plane Migration Capabilities:\n1. **Direct JSON Ingestion:** Accepts standard Plane export bundles via direct drag-and-drop file upload or pasting raw JSON.\n2. **Real-Time Entity Metric Cards:** Displays instant counts for detected Projects, States, Issues, Cycles, Modules, Issue Comments, and Members.\n3. **Stage 1 Dry-Run Simulation:** Simulates the complete import without writing to the database. Displays state mapping translations, identifies potential duplicate keys, and computes idempotency diffs.\n4. **Atomic Transactional Import:** Live migrations execute within an atomic transaction. If any entity fails validation or violates an object graph invariant, the entire migration rolls back cleanly, leaving existing data untouched.\n5. **Universal Link Synthesis:** Automatically establishes typed `PARENT_OF`, `BLOCKS`, and `ATTACHED_TO` object links corresponding to source Plane relationships.\n\n---\n\n## Emergency Rollback Procedure\n\nIf a critical business blocker occurs during the cutover window:\n1. **Revert DNS:** Immediately restore DNS routing to the legacy tracker cluster.\n2. **Delta Capture:** Run `uv run kanban-ctl cutover verify` / inspect `activity_records` since cutover to extract any tickets updated in \ud83d\udc4dkanban during the live window.\n3. **Reconcile:** Re-apply the delta diff into the source tracker to ensure zero data loss.\n\n![Workspace Home After Successful Cutover](images/05-workspace-home.png)\n"
+    "content": "# [Guide] Legacy Tracker Migration and Cutover Runbook\n\n## Overview\n\nOrganizations seeking to escape SaaS paywalls, Jira seat taxes, and single-vendor agent lock-in require a safe, deterministic migration path. Legacy project management tools often store data in proprietary formats, making manual migration prone to data loss, dropped comments, and broken ticket linkages.\n\n\ud83d\udc4dkanban provides a battle-tested **7-Phase Live Cutover Protocol** (`docs/CUTOVER.md`) designed for migrating from legacy issue trackers (such as Jira, Vibe Kanban, or self-hosted boards) to \ud83d\udc4dkanban with zero data loss and minimal operational disruption.\n\n---\n\n## The 7-Phase Live Cutover Protocol\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    P1[\"Phase 1: Pre-Cutover Readiness & Schema Alignment<br/>- Deploy target stack, configure Multi-Card Auth<br/>- Run healthchecks and verify checksums\"]\n    P2[\"Phase 2: Read-Only Freeze of Source Platform<br/>- Place legacy tracker in maintenance mode<br/>- Capture baseline snapshot\"]\n    P3[\"Phase 3: Extraction & Markdown Normalization<br/>- Ingest JSON/XML export<br/>- Run Unicode Surrogate & Paste-Jacking pipeline\"]\n    P4[\"Phase 4: Universal Object Graph Hydration & Linking<br/>- Populate UOG spine & typed object_links<br/>- Generate redirect aliases\"]\n    P5[\"Phase 5: Six Non-Bypassable Verification Gates<br/>- Entity counts, Link Auditor, Markdown fidelity,<br/>ACL parity, MCP health, SLA latency\"]\n    P6[\"Phase 6: DNS Cutover & Traffic Switch<br/>- Point domain to \ud83d\udc4dkanban Caddy ingress\"]\n    P7[\"Phase 7: Post-Cutover Monitoring & Rollback Window<br/>- 7-day read-only fallback window\"]\n\n    P1 --> P2\n    P2 --> P3\n    P3 --> P4\n    P4 --> P5\n    P5 -->|Certified PASSED| P6\n    P6 --> P7\n```\n\n![Standalone to Production Compose Export](images/27-standalone-compose-export.png)\n\n### Phase 1: Pre-Cutover Readiness and Schema Alignment\n- Deploy target \ud83d\udc4dkanban production stack.\n- Configure Multi-Card Authentication cards to match source identity providers (OIDC/SAML/LDAP).\n- Run migration pre-flight checks: `uv run kanban-ctl ops healthcheck` and verify source export snapshot checksums (`sha256sum -c manifest.sha256`).\n\n### Phase 2: Read-Only Freeze of Source Platform\n- Place the legacy tracker instance into read-only maintenance mode.\n- Notify engineering teams and pause active CI/CD webhooks.\n- Capture baseline snapshot of source database.\n\n### Phase 3: Extraction and Markdown Normalization\n- Extract work items, cycles, modules, pages, stickies, and attachments via source tracker export APIs.\n- Pass all textual descriptions and comments through the \ud83d\udc4dkanban **Canonical Markdown Pipeline**:\n  - Rejects Unicode lone surrogates.\n  - Strips hidden DOM paste-jacking sequences.\n  - Converts legacy HTML into clean, standardized CommonMark.\n\n### Phase 4: Universal Object Graph Hydration\n- Ingest normalized objects into the PostgreSQL Universal Object Graph (`kanban_migrator`).\n- Translate legacy issue references (`PROJ-123`) into canonical \ud83d\udc4dkanban identifiers while creating redirect aliases.\n- Establish typed `object_links` for all parent-child relationships, sub-issues, and blockers.\n\n### Phase 5: The Six Non-Bypassable Verification Gates\nBefore DNS can be redirected, the migration must pass all 6 automated verification gates:\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    Gate1[\"Gate 1<br/>Entity Parity\"] --> Gate2[\"Gate 2<br/>Link Auditor\"]\n    Gate2 --> Gate3[\"Gate 3<br/>Markdown Fidelity\"]\n    Gate3 --> Gate4[\"Gate 4<br/>ACL Parity\"]\n    Gate4 --> Gate5[\"Gate 5<br/>MCP Health\"]\n    Gate5 --> Gate6[\"Gate 6<br/>SLA Latency\"]\n    Gate6 --> Cutover[\"Ready for Live Cutover\"]\n```\n\n| Gate # | Verification Gate | Success Threshold |\n| :---: | :--- | :--- |\n| **1** | **Entity Count Parity** | 100% match across issues, states, cycles, modules, comments, and attachments. |\n| **2** | **Object Link Auditor** | Zero orphaned links, cross-tenant leaks, or invalid hierarchy cycles. |\n| **3** | **Markdown Fidelity** | 100% of descriptions render valid Markdown; zero unparsed HTML tags. |\n| **4** | **Principal & ACL Parity** | All users, groups, and permissions map accurately to \ud83d\udc4dkanban roles. |\n| **5** | **MCP Surface Health** | All 24 MCP tools return clean schemas and pass handshake benchmarks. |\n| **6** | **Performance Latency** | Board view initial load under 100ms; REST API p95 latency under 50ms. |\n\n### Phase 6: DNS Cutover and Traffic Switch\n- Update internal DNS records or reverse proxy routing (e.g. Caddy / Nginx) to point domain `kanban.example.com` to the \ud83d\udc4dkanban production ingress (`edge_net`).\n- Restart agent background workers with updated MCP endpoint URLs.\n\n### Phase 7: Post-Cutover Monitoring and Rollback Window\n- Maintain legacy tracker instance in read-only state for a 7-day observation window.\n- Monitor real-time WebSocket connection stability and activity logs.\n\n---\n\n## Migration Import Studio (`/admin/imports`)\n\nTo streamline cutover from Plane workspaces to \ud83d\udc4dkanban without custom extraction scripts, \ud83d\udc4dkanban includes a native **Migration Import Studio** accessible at `/admin/imports` (and `/settings/mcp` -> Migration Studio tab).\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    subgraph PlaneImportPipeline[\"Migration Import Studio Pipeline\"]\n        Upload[\"Step 1: Upload Plane Export Bundle<br/>(File upload or paste raw JSON)\"] --> Parse[\"JSON Schema Validation<br/>Verify projects, states, issues, cycles, modules, comments, members\"]\n        Parse --> Metrics[\"Step 2: Entity Detection & Metrics Cards<br/>Live counts across all 7 entity types\"]\n        Metrics --> DryRun[\"Step 3: Stage 1 Dry-Run Simulation<br/>Idempotency checks, state mapping preview, conflict detection\"]\n        DryRun --> Live[\"Step 4: Execute Live Migration<br/>Atomic PostgreSQL transaction (kanban_migrator)\"]\n        Live --> Verify[\"Step 5: Post-Import Integrity Audit<br/>Run Invalid Object Link Auditor on imported graph\"]\n    end\n```\n\n![Migration Import Studio Step 1](images/49-admin-plane-import-studio.png)\n\n![Migration Studio Dry-Run Simulation](images/71-plane-migration-dry-run.png)\n\n### Key Migration Capabilities:\n1. **Direct JSON Ingestion:** Accepts standard Plane export bundles via direct drag-and-drop file upload or pasting raw JSON.\n2. **Real-Time Entity Metric Cards:** Displays instant counts for detected Projects, States, Issues, Cycles, Modules, Issue Comments, and Members.\n3. **Stage 1 Dry-Run Simulation:** Simulates the complete import without writing to the database. Displays state mapping translations, identifies potential duplicate keys, and computes idempotency diffs.\n4. **Atomic Transactional Import:** Live migrations execute within an atomic transaction. If any entity fails validation or violates an object graph invariant, the entire migration rolls back cleanly, leaving existing data untouched.\n5. **Universal Link Synthesis:** Automatically establishes typed `PARENT_OF`, `BLOCKS`, and `ATTACHED_TO` object links corresponding to source Plane relationships.\n\n---\n\n## Emergency Rollback Procedure\n\nIf a critical business blocker occurs during the cutover window:\n1. **Revert DNS:** Immediately restore DNS routing to the legacy tracker cluster.\n2. **Delta Capture:** Run `uv run kanban-ctl cutover verify` / inspect `activity_records` since cutover to extract any tickets updated in \ud83d\udc4dkanban during the live window.\n3. **Reconcile:** Re-apply the delta diff into the source tracker to ensure zero data loss.\n\n![Workspace Home After Successful Cutover](images/05-workspace-home.png)\n"
