   API->>DB: SELECT * FROM issues WHERE key = 'JIRA-101'\n    DB-->>API: 0 rows returned\n    API->>DB: SELECT canonical_key FROM issue_key_aliases WHERE legacy_key = 'JIRA-101'\n    DB-->>API: 1 row returned ('KAN-42')\n    API-->>Client: HTTP 308 Permanent Redirect (Location: /api/v1/issues/KAN-42)\n    Client->>API: GET /api/v1/issues/KAN-42\n    API->>DB: SELECT * FROM issues WHERE key = 'KAN-42'\n    DB-->>API: Issue payload\n    API-->>Client: HTTP 200 OK\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Cross-Project Merge Mode (`KANBA -> KAN`)\n\nDuring organizational consolidations, teams frequently need to merge entire projects into a single target project. The cross-project merge mode executes this consolidation losslessly:\n\n### Merge Execution Steps\n1. **Entity Re-Keying:** Each issue from the source project is re-keyed to the destination project prefix (e.g. `KANBA-15` becomes `KAN-248`), with sequence numbers allocated sequentially to avoid collisions.\n2. **Alias Registration:** The original key (`KANBA-15`) is recorded in `issue_key_aliases` pointing to the new issue ID.\n3. **Object Link Rewiring:** All directional relations (`PARENT_OF`, `BLOCKS`, `RELATES_TO`) in `object_links` pointing to the old issue are updated in place.\n4. **State Taxonomy Mapping:** Workflow states from the source project are mapped to equivalent states in the target project via an interactive alignment table.\n5. **Activity Log Continuity:** Historical audit entries are preserved and appended with a merge marker documenting the consolidation event.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Canonical CSV Import, Export, and Password-Protected ZIP (AES-256) Packaging\n\nTicket `KAN-316` establishes enterprise CSV data interchange governance across system, workspace, and role tiers:\n\n### 16 Canonical CSV Columns\n\nExports and imports follow a deterministic 16-column RFC 4180 layout:\n1. `key`: Canonical issue key (e.g. `KAN-42`).\n2. `project_key`: Target project identifier.\n3. `summary`: Concise issue title.\n4. `descript